**How to implement.** The plan is emitted into the kit as setups and experiments of role `PlannedRun`, so plan → measure → attach → fit is one object model (001 §M 'a measurement plan emitted as setups + experiments with role `Planned` into the same kit'; 001 §O 'Plan view: … with "Add to kit"'; the S14.2 brief). A candidate is added over the window's table as the grid generator adds a combination (step 276), REUSING its body: the candidate's plate goes into the table's Object 1 slot, its experiment is the draft's own commit over the setup (step 275), and the role is set as `SetExperimentRole` sets it (step 294). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `GenerateSetupGrid`'s arm body (step 276, which records through step 278's two private functions) becomes a private function of the update taking the grid, the collection to commit from and the role its appended experiments take (`Experiment.withRole`, step 294, before each is recorded) and answering the model with what was written, the setups and the appended experiments; `GenerateSetupGrid grid` calls it with the window's collection and `ScienceRun` and keeps its texts and outcomes, so `SetupModelTests`' facts (step 276) hold unchanged. (2) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `AddPlannedExperiment of PlanCandidate`, documented in one line, refused by step 185's read-only guard and otherwise, in order: the table's Object 1 slot (`ObjectSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)` of `SetupSlot.inLightOrder model.elements`, step 257), none setting `kitStatus` to `Not added — the table has no sample slot.`; the candidate already in the kit (`coverageIn model.kitSetups model.experimentCollection.experiments`, step 482) setting `Not added — <the experiment's name> already plans it.`; the candidate's `capture` not among `availableCaptures model <the slot's id>` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:availableCaptures`) setting `Not added — no detector of the table captures the transmitted light of the sample.` (or `reflected`); otherwise the function of (1) over the grid `SetupGrid.create [ { slot = <the slot's id>; choices = [ { itemOpt = Some candidate.plate.item; r1 = Angle.zero } ] } ] model.elements model.kitItems model.tryItemModelChoice` (step 274: a held setup of equal slots is reused, a new one named by the template), the collection whose draft is built from `ExperimentDraft.empty` (`Experiments.fs:ExperimentDraft`) by the draft's own functions — `chooseElement` of the slot's id, its `experimentElementLabel`, `[ VaryR2 ]` and the capture (`Experiments.fs:chooseElement`), `setRange PlanCandidate.incidenceRange`, `addScanAxis` (step 288), `chooseElement` again with `[ VaryR1 ]`, `setRange PlanCandidate.azimuthRange` and `chooseMeasurement candidate.capture` — so its scan is the one block `coverageIn` reads, and `PlannedRun`; then the window's own draft is put back. Success sets `kitStatus` to `Planned <the experiment's name> over <the setup reference's describe>.`; a grid that cannot be made, or a write that fails, keeps step 276's texts (`Not generated — …`, `Not saved to the kit — …`). An added experiment is removed as any experiment is, through the Experiments bay's Remove (step 152), so Add to kit needs no undo of its own (.spec-md §10.5). No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `PlanWindowModelTests` (step 488), over its kit with the Polarimeter assigned to the inverse table's `det`: `Add to kit records the candidate's setup and a planned experiment sweeping its angles on its branch`: `AddPlannedExperiment` of QZ-Z's transmitted candidate leaves the kit holding a setup whose `sample` slot holds QZ-Z and an experiment over it whose role is `PlannedRun` and whose `coverageIn` answers `CandidateInKit` of it, `kitStatus` starting `Planned `, and the window's draft unchanged. `a candidate the kit already holds is not added again`: adding it again writes no file, leaves the kit's setups and experiments as they were and sets `kitStatus` to `Not added — <the experiment's name> already plans it.`. `a candidate the table cannot capture, or a table with no sample slot, adds nothing, and a read-only kit adds nothing`: the reflected candidate over the default table (`det` on the transmitted beam alone) writes nothing and names the reflected light; a table with its sample removed writes nothing and says `no sample slot`; over the kit opened read-only nothing is written and `kitStatus` is the guard's. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After Add to kit lands, `AddPlannedExperiment` MUST record the candidate's plate in the table's Object 1 slot as a setup and a `PlannedRun` experiment sweeping its R2 then R1 ranges on its branch through the grid generator's own recording, refuse a candidate the kit holds, a branch no detector captures, a table with no sample slot and a read-only kit, and leave `GenerateSetupGrid` unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `Add to kit records the candidate's setup and a planned experiment sweeping its angles on its branch`, `a candidate the kit already holds is not added again` and `a candidate the table cannot capture, or a table with no sample slot, adds nothing, and a read-only kit adds nothing`, the count rising by 3, and `SetupModelTests` unchanged; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.
